  "body": "## Lines of code\nhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/main/ve33/contracts/GovernanceHYBR.sol#L41\n\n## Vulnerability details\n\n### Impact\n\nThe `head_not_withdraw_time` variable at line 41 has a critical value/comment mismatch. The comment indicates \"5days\" but the actual value is **1200 seconds (20 minutes)**, creating a **360x error factor**. This severely undermines governance security by allowing head position withdrawal after only 20 minutes instead of the intended 5 days.\n\n**Security Impact:**\n- Users can withdraw from head position **4 days, 23 hours, 40 minutes earlier** than intended\n- Maximum head turnovers increase from **6/month (intended)** to **2,160/month (actual)**\n- Governance lock mechanism completely defeated\n- Protocol stability compromised by rapid head rotation\n- Attackers can game governance with minimal commitment (20 min vs 5 days)\n\n**Mathematical Proof:**\n\nCurrent value: 1,200 seconds = 20 minutes\nIntended value: 432,000 seconds = 5 days\nError factor: 432,000 / 1,200 = 360x too small\nPremature withdrawal: 430,800 seconds (4.98 days) early\n\n### Proof of Concept\n\n**Vulnerable Code (Line 41):**\n\n// File: ve33/contracts/GovernanceHYBR.sol\n// Line 41\n\nuint256 public head_not_withdraw_time = 1200; // 5days\n\n**Mathematical PoC Results** (from test execution):\n\n=== M-04: GovernanceHYBR Time Window Configuration Error ===\n\nVULNERABLE CODE:\nuint256 public head_not_withdraw_time = 1200; // 5days\n\n=== TIME ANALYSIS ===\nCurrent value: 1200 seconds\nCurrent value in minutes: 20\nCurrent value in hours: 0\nCurrent value in days: 0\n\nIntended value (from comment '5days'): 432000 seconds\nIntended value in days: 5\n\n=== ERROR MAGNITUDE ===\nError factor: 360 x too small\nDifference: 430800 seconds\nDifference in days: 4\n\n=== HEAD TURNOVER RATE COMPARISON ===\nWith CURRENT value (20 min):\nMax head turnovers per month: 2160\nGovernance UNSTABLE - too frequent changes\n\nWith INTENDED value (5 days):\nMax head turnovers per month: 6\nGovernance STABLE - reasonable lock period\n\nIMPACT:\nBug allows 2160 x more turnovers than intended\nDefeats purpose of governance lock mechanism\n\n## To run PoC:\n\n~/2025-10-hybra-finance/ve33$ \nforge test --match-contract M04_GovernanceHYBR_TimeWindow_Mathematical_PoC -vvv\n\n## Expected output :\n\n[⠔] Compiling...\nNo files changed, compilation skipped\n\nRan 4 tests for test/M04_GovernanceHYBR_TimeWindow_Mathematical_PoC.t.sol:M04_GovernanceHYBR_TimeWindow_Mathematical_PoC\n[PASS] test_CodeCommentMismatch() (gas: 18557)\nLogs:\n  === CODE vs COMMENT ANALYSIS ===\n  \n  SOURCE CODE:\n    uint256 public head_not_withdraw_time = 1200; // 5days\n  \n  COMMENT INTERPRETATION:\n    '5days' clearly indicates intention\n    Standard Solidity time units: 1 days = 86400 seconds\n    5 days = 5 * 86400 = 432000 seconds\n  \n  ACTUAL VALUE:\n    1200 seconds = 0.0139 days\n  \n  CONCLUSION:\n    Clear mismatch between intention (comment) and implementation (value)\n    Developer likely intended: uint256 public head_not_withdraw_time = 5 days;\n    Or with explicit calculation: uint256 public head_not_withdraw_time = 432000;\n  \n  RECOMMENDED FIX:\n    uint256 public head_not_withdraw_time = 5 days; // 5 days (432000 seconds)\n\n[PASS] test_MultipleHeadTurnoverScenario() (gas: 13123)\nLogs:\n  === HEAD TURNOVER RATE COMPARISON ===\n  \n  With CURRENT value (20 min):\n    Max head turnovers per month: 2160\n    Governance UNSTABLE - too frequent changes\n  \n  With INTENDED value (5 days):\n    Max head turnovers per month: 6\n    Governance STABLE - reasonable lock period\n  \n  IMPACT:\n    Bug allows 2160 x more turnovers than intended\n    Defeats purpose of governance lock mechanism\n\n[PASS] test_SecurityImplicationsDemonstration() (gas: 21009)\nLogs:\n  === SECURITY IMPLICATIONS ===\n  \n  1. GOVERNANCE ATTACK SURFACE:\n     - Attacker can become head\n     - Wait only 20 minutes instead of 5 days\n     - Withdraw 